<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodore Rshtuni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 655</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodore Rshtuni (died 655) was an Armenian prince and military commander who led the defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> against the first Arab raids. In 653 he made a treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muawiya-i">Muawiya</a>, then governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, accepting Arab overlordship in return for autonomy and the right to keep Armenian troops, and he was recognised as prince of Armenia. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> in 655.</p></div>
